  "description": {
   "value": "<p><strong>Upgrade DV:</strong> DV 24<br>\n<strong>Cost:</strong> Cost #1: Cost of the most expensive component Skill Chips.\n\nCost #2: 1,000eb<br>\n<strong>Thermometer:</strong> Increases Skills in a manner that\ndoes not stack with existing Skill increases.<br>\n<strong>Applies To:</strong> Skill Chips<br>\n<strong>Vendor:</strong> WebMynx</p>\n<p>\"Compressing the data on these things is more neuro-art than neuro-science. Standard compression algorithms are too lossy, so you gotta try a few custom ones and tweak it here and there to get it just right. Fun little puzzle.\"</p>\n<p>Double Chip combines two Skill Chips into a single item with a Humanity Loss of 7 (2d6). When slotted into a Chipware Socket, the user gains the benefit of both component Skill Chips. If the two component Skill Chips were made for the same Skill, the user gains that Skill at a +4 instead of a +3. The two component Skill Chips must be acquired separately before being combined.</p>\n<p><strong>Enhances:</strong> Skill Chip</p>\n<p><strong>Foundry notes:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Price is Cost #2 only; Cost #1 is the cost of the more expensive Skill Chip.</li>\n<li>Combining the chips is done by hand: give the Skill Chip the second skill, and Humanity Loss 7 (2d6).</li>\n</ul>\n<p><em>From Bontari Homebrew Cyberpunk Items by Bontari (Invented Tech Upgrades).</em></p>"
  },
